  "worked_solution": "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{2}x+3\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=-\\frac{1}{2}y+3\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-\\frac{1}{2}y+3 \\\\ x-3 & =-\\frac{1}{2}y \\\\ -2(x-3) & =y \\\\ -2x+6 & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=-2x+6\n$$",
